\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 45\u00b0F, and the record is 70\u00b0F (1953, 2016). The low of <strong>25\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Mobridge's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Mobridge has set <strong>51 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 92 that chance alone would give, and <strong>90 record highs</strong>, close to the 92 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (89). Mobridge's all-time high is 116\u00b0F, on July 16, 1936.","t_chg":"Mobridge's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 97 complete years: Mobridge's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.22\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.34), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1911. Mobridge's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.06\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.23 to +0.11) that includes zero. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months; April fell. Highs rose in none; 4 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Mobridge's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.10 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 17.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 2019 (29.51 in); the driest, 1934 (6.15 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}